.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "January 2026" "Holberton School" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simple_shell \- a simple UNIX command interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simple_shell
.br
.B ./hsh

.SH DESCRIPTION
simple_shell is a simple UNIX command line interpreter.
It reads commands from standard input and executes them.

The shell works in both interactive and non-interactive modes.
In interactive mode, a prompt is displayed and the shell waits
for user input.
In non-interactive mode, commands are read from standard input
without displaying a prompt.

Command lines may contain a command name and arguments separated
by spaces.

.SH BUILTINS
The following built-in commands are supported:

.TP
.B env
Prints the current environment.

.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell.

.TP
.B osokour
Exits the shell.

.SH USAGE
Interactive mode:
.br
.RS
$ ./hsh
.br
shellobscur$ ls
.br
shellobscur$ exit
.RE

Non-interactive mode:
.br
.RS
$ echo "ls" | ./hsh
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS
simple_shell returns the exit status of the last executed command.
If a command is not found, the shell returns 127.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
The shell uses the PATH environment variable to locate executables.
If PATH is not set, a default path of /bin:/usr/bin is used.

.SH AUTHOR
Written by Mateo Marques and Benjamin Bommier
